          "en": "A short story"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Ravi looked at a map and saw the Himalayas in the north and the sea in the south.\n\"India has many landforms,\" said his teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "Himalayas",
          "plateau",
          "coastal plain"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "India has six physical divisions: the Northern Mountains (Himalayas), the Northern Plains, the Peninsular Plateau, the Thar Desert, the Coastal Plains and the Islands.\nThe Himalayas have snow-capped peaks and give rise to rivers like the Ganga. The Northern Plains are fertile.\nThe Western and Eastern Ghats lie along the coasts of the plateau."
        }
      },
